SUMMARY:Robotics Graduate Studies Information Session
DESCRIPTION:Interested in a master’s or PhD in robotics? Join the Robotics Institute and the University of Toronto Robotics Association (UTRA) to explore graduate research opportunities at the University of Toronto. \nMeet faculty and current graduate students\, learn about the cutting-edge robotics research happening across the university\, and get tips for submitting a strong application. \n\nStudents will have the opportunity to learn more about research opportunities in the following labs: \n\nCLIMB Lab directed by Professor Pakpong Chirarattananon\nData-Driven Decision Making Lab (D3M Lab) directed by Professor Scott Sanner\nSpace and Terrestrial Autonomous Robotics Systems Lab (STARS Lab) directed by Professor Jonathan Kelly\nToronto Intelligent Systems Lab (TISL Lab) directed by Professor Igor Gilitschenski\nToronto Robotics & AI Systems Lab (TRAIL Lab) directed by Professor Steven Waslander\n\nRSVP by November 4. Pizza to be provided!
URL:https://www.engineering.utoronto.ca/event/robotics-graduate-studies-information-session/
LOCATION:Myhal Centre for Engineering Innovation & Entrepreneurship\, Room 580\, 55 St. George Street\, Toronto\, Ontario\, M5S 0C9\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Info sessions
END:VEVENT
