SUMMARY:ECE Lecture Series: Professor Peyman Mohajerin Esfahani
DESCRIPTION:Anomaly Detection for Nonlinear Dynamical Systems: Tractable Algorithms with Probabilistic Guarantees\nJoin ECE for a guest lecture by Professor Peyman Mohajerin Esfahani\, Associate Professor at the University of Toronto. \nAbstract\nIn this seminar\, we study a broad class of anomaly/fault detection for large-scale nonlinear dynamical systems. Noting a connection between the diagnosis filter and the so-called behavioral sets of dynamical systems\, we leverage tools from traditional model-based approaches and modern data-driven analytics to address the inherent complexity of the problem. We also discuss probabilistic guarantees for the proposed design. The discussion will be motivated by applications in power system security\, autonomous vehicles\, and leakage detection in water distribution networks. \nBiography\nProfessor Peyman Mohajerin Esfahani is an Associate Professor at the University of Toronto\, where he joined in 2025. Prior to that\, he was a faculty member at Delft University of Technology\, having joined in 2016 following several research appointments at EPFL\, ETH Zurich\, and MIT between 2014 and 2016. He received the PhD degree from ETH Zurich\, Switzerland\, and the MSc and BSc degrees from Sharif University of Technology\, Iran. His research interests include theoretical and practical aspects of decision-making problems in uncertain and dynamic environments\, with applications in engineering systems and management. \nHe currently serves as an associate editor of Operations Research\, Transactions on Automatic Control\, Mathematical Programming\, Mathematics of Operations Research\, and Open Journal of Mathematical Optimization. He was one of the three finalists for the Young Researcher Prize in Continuous Optimization awarded by the Mathematical Optimization Society in 2016\, and a recipient of the 2016 George S. Axelby Outstanding Paper Award from the IEEE Control Systems Society. He received the ERC Starting Grant and the INFORMS Frederick W. Lanchester Prize in 2020. He is the recipient of the 2022 European Control Award.
URL:https://www.engineering.utoronto.ca/event/ece-lecture-series-professor-peyman-mohajerin-esfahani/
LOCATION:Galbraith Building\, Room 202 (GB202)\, 35 St George\, Toronto\, Ontario\, M5S 1A4\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Lectures, seminars and workshops
END:VEVENT
