SUMMARY:Exploring the Undergrad Research Journey – A Lunch & Learn Conversation with Professor Bentz
DESCRIPTION:Date: Monday\, November 23\, 2026\nTime: 12:00pm to 1:00pm\nLocation: In-person: GB202\, Galbraith Building\, Room 202\, 35 St. George St.\, 2nd floor  \nInterested in engineering research and learning where to begin as an undergrad student? Join us for a lunch & learn conversation with Professor Evan Bentz (Professor\, Civil Engineering\, and Vice-Dean\, Undergraduate) to explore what undergraduate research is: what is the value\, what to expect\, and how it can help with future engineering careers in research or in industry. We’ll also cover tips on how to begin finding research placements and funding opportunities.   \nPizza refreshments provided! Please register here.  \nQuestions? Please email undergrad.research@engineering.utoronto.ca  
