SUMMARY:Disruptors & Dilemmas — Surviving the smoke: The new reality of wildfires
DESCRIPTION:Register now!   \nWildfires are no longer distant events unfolding deep in remote forests. As fires grow more frequent and intense\, their impacts are increasingly felt in our cities\, communities and the air we breathe. How do wildfires reshape the future of our forests\, cities and climate? \nJoin University of Toronto experts for an engaging discussion on the science\, technology and human realities of wildfires. Explore how robotics and aerial monitoring are changing the way fires are tracked\, why wildfire smoke poses growing challenges for urban centres and how communities can adapt in a world where fire is both a natural part of the landscape and an escalating public concern. \nFrom public health and environmental justice to urban planning and climate resilience\, discover how the decisions we make today will shape our ability to live with fire tomorrow. \nThis is a Disruptors and Dilemmas speaker series event.This event is co-hosted by: University of Toronto Faculty of Applied Science and Engineering\, Temerty Faculty of Medicine and University of Toronto Mississauga. \nHave a question for one of our panelists? Submit it on the registration page. \nAbout the speakers \n \nProfessor Steven Waslander  \nProfessor\, Institute for Aerospace Studies\, U of TDirector\, U of T Robotics Institute\, U of T   \nProfessor Samir Gupta  \nAssociate Professor\, Department of Medicine\,U of T  \nScientist\, Li Ka Shing Knowledge Institute of St. Michael’s Hospital  \n \nUniversity Professor Kent Moore  \nProfessor\, Chemical and Physical Sciences\, UTM  \nAssociate Scientist\, University of Washington Applied Physics Laboratory  \nOur moderator \n \nProfessor Marianne Hatzopoulou  \nChair\, Department of Civil & Mineral Engineering   \nTier 1 Canada Research Chair in Transport Decarbonization and Air Quality   \nDirector\, Positive Zero Transport Futures   \nHead of the Transportation and Air Quality research group (TRAQ) \nProudly sponsored by U of T affinity partners: \n   \nDiscover the benefits of affinity products!
URL:https://www.engineering.utoronto.ca/event/surviving-the-smoke-the-new-reality-of-wildfires/
LOCATION:Online
CATEGORIES:Lectures, seminars and workshops
END:VEVENT
